474 - Take the Name of Jesus With You
 / 
Key: Ab
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 474
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Ab]Take the name of Jesus with you,
[Db]Child of sorrow and of [Ab]woe;
[Eb7]It will joy and comfort [Ab]give you,
[Eb7]Take it, where’er you [Ab]go.
Precious [Db]name, O how [Ab]sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [Eb]heaven;
[Eb7]Precious [Ab]name, O how [Db]sweet!
Hope of [Ab]earth and [Eb7]joy of [Ab]heaven.

Refrain:
[Ab]Precious Name, O how sweet!
[Db]Hope of earth [Ab]and joy of Heav'n.
[Eb7]Precious Name, [Ab]O how sweet!
[Eb7]Hope of earth [Ab]and joy of Heav'n.

Verse 2:
[Ab]Take the Name of Jesus ever,
[Db]As a shield [Ab]from every snare;
[Eb7]If temptations [Ab]round you gather,
[Eb7]Breathe that holy [Ab]Name in prayer.

Verse 3:
[Ab]O the precious Name of Jesus!
[Db]How it thrills [Ab]our souls with joy,
[Eb7]When His loving [Ab]arms receive us,
[Eb7]And His songs [Ab]our tongues employ!

Verse 4:
[Ab]At the Name of Jesus bowing,
[Db]Falling prostrate [Ab]at His feet,
[Eb7]King of kings in [Ab]heav'n we'll crown Him,
[Eb7]When our [Ab]journey is complete.
